#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:7
msgid "Earth Magnetic Anomaly Model (EMAG2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:8
msgid "World Digital Magnetic Anomaly Map (WDMAM)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:12
msgid ""
"This function downloads the dataset from the GMT data server, caches it in a "
"user data directory (usually ``~/.gmt/server/earth/earth_mag/``, ``~/.gmt/"
"server/earth/earth_mag4km/``, ``~/.gmt/server/earth/earth_wdmam/``), and "
"load the dataset as an :class:`xarray.DataArray`. An internet connection is "
"required the first time around, but subsequent calls will load the dataset "
"from the local data directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:19
msgid ""
"The dataset can also be accessed by specifying a file name in any grid "
"processing function or plotting method, using the following file name "
"format: **@**\\ *earth_mag_type*\\_\\ *res*\\_\\ *reg*. *earth_mag_type* is "
"the GMT name for the dataset. The available options are **earth_mag**, "
"**earth_mag4km**, and **earth_wdmam**; *res* is the grid resolution; *reg* "
"is the grid registration type (**p** for pixel registration, **g** for "
"gridline registration). If *reg* is omitted (e.g., ``@earth_mag_01d``), the "
"gridline-registered grid will be loaded for grid processing functions and "
"the pixel-registered grid will be loaded for plotting functions. If *res* is "
"also omitted (i.e., ``@earth_mag``), GMT automatically selects a suitable "
"resolution based on the current region and projection settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:31
msgid ""
"The default color palette tables (CPTs) for this dataset are ``@earth_mag."
"cpt`` for ``data_source=\"emag2\"`` and ``data_source=\"emag2_4km\"``, and "
"``@earth_wdmam.cpt`` for ``data_source=\"wdmam\"``. To use the dataset-"
"specific CPT when plotting the dataset, explicitly set ``cmap=\"@earth_mag."
"cpt\"`` or ``cmap=\"@earth_wdmam.cpt\"``, otherwise GMT's default CPT "
"(*google/turbo*) will be used. If the dataset is referenced by the file name "
"in a grid plotting method, the dataset-specific CPT file is used "
"automatically unless another CPT is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:39
msgid ""
"Refer to :gmt-datasets:`earth-mag.html` and :gmt-datasets:`earth-wdmam.html` "
"for more details about available datasets, including version information and "
"references."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:43
msgid ""
"The grid resolution. The suffix ``d`` and ``m`` stand for arc-degrees and "
"arc-minutes. The resolution ``\"02m\"`` is not available for "
"``data_source=\"wdmam\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:47
msgid ""
"The subregion of the grid to load, in the form of a sequence [*xmin*, "
"*xmax*, *ymin*, *ymax*] or an ISO country code. Required for grids with "
"resolutions higher than 5 arc-minutes (i.e., ``\"05m\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:51
msgid ""
"Grid registration type. Either ``\"pixel\"`` for pixel registration or "
"``\"gridline\"`` for gridline registration. Default is ``None``, which means "
"``\"gridline\"`` for all resolutions except ``\"02m\"`` for "
"``data_source=\"emag2\"`` or ``data_source=\"emag2_4km\"``, which are "
"``\"pixel\"`` only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:57
msgid ""
"Select the source of the magnetic anomaly data. Available options are:  - "
"``\"emag2\"``: EMAG2 Earth Magnetic Anomaly Model. It only includes   data "
"observed at sea level over oceanic regions.   See :gmt-datasets:`earth-mag."
"html`. - ``\"emag2_4km\"``: Use a version of EMAG2 where all observations   "
"are relative to an altitude of 4 km above the geoid and include   data over "
"land. - ``\"wdmam\"``: World Digital Magnetic Anomaly Map (WDMAM).   See :"
"gmt-datasets:`earth-wdmam.html`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:57
msgid "Select the source of the magnetic anomaly data. Available options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:59
msgid ""
"``\"emag2\"``: EMAG2 Earth Magnetic Anomaly Model. It only includes data "
"observed at sea level over oceanic regions. See :gmt-datasets:`earth-mag."
"html`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:62
msgid ""
"``\"emag2_4km\"``: Use a version of EMAG2 where all observations are "
"relative to an altitude of 4 km above the geoid and include data over land."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/datasets/earth_magnetic_anomaly.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.datasets.earth_magnetic_anomaly.load_earth_magnetic_anomaly:65
msgid ""
"``\"wdmam\"``: World Digital Magnetic Anomaly Map (WDMAM). See :gmt-datasets:"
"`earth-wdmam.html`."
msgstr ""

